Z||000002||TwisT||04-22-2000||06:44 PM||||Foliatech sells actual brake-caliper painting kits,  which uses a laquer-based paint and cleaner.  Problem is you have to search for a distributor,  because Foliatech is a European company...  look in your local magazine rack to find an issue of Super Street or Sport Compact Car.<P>Personally,  I think painting brake calipers is a great little detail job that can really show off a car's stopping goods. <P>Paint away!  ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Monkeyman||04-22-2000||10:36 PM||||We've discussed this before but just remember the paint color vs. hp rules.  <BR>Yellow calipers gets you an additional 15 hp.<BR>Red calipers get you 10 hp.<BR>Any other color will only get you 5-7 hp.||||reg||1
Z||000004||TwisT||04-22-2000||11:33 PM||||Yes,  Monkeyman...  but what if you color-match your calipers to your existing body color?  Should be some extra ponies there.  <P>Anyone up for a dyno comparison???||||reg||1
Z||000005||GT Bastard||04-23-2000||12:41 AM||||Well, you only get an extra gain from that if you attach a coffee can to your exhaust pipe!||||reg||1
Z||000006||Racer 1||04-23-2000||12:54 AM||||A sticker here and there aint gona hurt nothing either! <P>I painted my calipers red I guess im a fast MTF! I used hIgH tEmP eNgInE pAiNt!||||reg||10
Z||000007||Spyder||04-23-2000||12:57 AM||||Clean calipers<BR>Prime with high temp primer (engine primer)<BR>With your favorite color of high temp engine paint, paint the calipers with about 5 coats in an hour let dry overnight or longer. Better yet follow directions on the can.<BR>Optional: Add several coats of clear coat via high temp engine clear coat paint. Follow directions on the can.<BR>The paint can be found at most auto parts stores.<BR>There you go.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.markalexandermiller.com/suspensionpaint.jpg"> <BR>Horse Power Gains Vary On Paint Color….and coats of paint.||||reg||1
Z||000008||iplayazi||04-23-2000||12:18 PM||||Im not a ricer  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I finished painting them and they look good.. I got gm matched paint to my car.. Identical to my paint job.. I was impressed. thanks for the info guys I appreciate it.||||reg||1
Z||000009||TwisT||04-23-2000||01:42 PM||||Spyder,  I see you have braided brake lines.  I've heard this really improves brake performance and pedal feel.<P>Did you have similiar results?  The painting job looks great.  =)||||reg||1
Z||000010||Cooter||04-23-2000||02:47 PM||||I have considered starting a sideline business of Metallic/Ceramic coatings. One of the available performance coatings is a thermal dispersant. This coating aids in removing heat from a part. It can be used on brake calipers, oil pans, intake manifolds and other heat generating pieces. The bad thing- it is only available in black.||||reg||1
Z||000011||87ECO5||04-23-2000||08:51 PM||||Don't forget that adding lettering to the calipers (a la Corvette or Porsche) adds a few ponies too!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000012||Standard||04-24-2000||03:38 AM||||I just ordered a set of earl's braided steel lines from the Fiero Store around $95 including shipping.. it was cheaper than buying 4 new rubber hoses at about $25 bucks each.  <P>Cooter - could I get some more info about that coating?  I've been thinking about painting my calipers and the only color I want to do it in would be black.. ||||reg||1
